---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import glyph from '../brand/glyph.svg?raw';
const goals = [
  'Run it yourself, in your own Cloudflare account.',
  'Nothing else to host or look after.',
  'Fill in the week, submit it, get it approved.',
  'Your data exports to common formats, any time.',
  'Committed to being open source.',
];
const features = [
  'A weekly grid with a note on each cell, and keyboard entry.',
  'Submit, return with a reason, approve and lock, with a list of who has not submitted.',
  'On-screen reports and a chart by person, client, project, task and week.',
  'CSV export, and an import that previews before it writes.',
  'Add, offboard and reinstate people; only admins create clients and projects.',
  'Passkeys, optional single sign-on, recovery codes and an admin rescue link.',
  'Nightly encrypted backups to a second account, with a status page and a test alert.',
  'An agent (MCP) surface, off unless you turn it on.',
  'Limits you set as deploy variables.',
];
---
<Layout title="tidwick: weekly timesheets you run yourself" description="Weekly timesheets you run yourself, in your own Cloudflare account.">
  <div class="top">
  <section class="hero">
    <Fragment set:html={glyph} />
    <p class="kicker">weekly timesheets you run yourself</p>
    <h1>tidwick</h1>
    <p class="deck">Weekly timesheets you run yourself.</p>
    <div class="ctas">
      <a class="cta primary" href="https://demo.tidwick.dev">Try the demo</a>
      <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick">Run your own</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="goals">
    <h2 id="goals">Design goals</h2>
    <ol class="goals">
      {goals.map((g, i) => <li><span class="num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span>{g}</span></li>)}
    </ol>
  </section>
  </div>
  <section aria-labelledby="features" class="features">
    <h2 id="features">What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      {features.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
  <div class="tiles">
    <section class="tile">
      <h2>Try the demo</h2>
      <p>A running copy you can look around in. Pick a person, no sign-up. It resets every night.</p>
      <p><a href="https://demo.tidwick.dev/demo">Open demo.tidwick.dev</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="tile">
      <h2>Run your own</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#9-deploy">docs walk through</a> deploying tidwick to your own Cloudflare account. It needs a Cloudflare account on the Workers Paid plan, and a second account for the off-account backup.</p>
      <p class="deploy">
        <a class="deploy-btn" href="https://deploy.workers.cloudflare.com/?url=https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick"><img src="/deploy-to-cloudflare.svg" alt="Deploy to Cloudflare" width="184" height="39" /></a>
      </p>
      <p>After deploying, open the new Worker's address. The setup page generates the keys in your browser, then a one-time setup token claims the first admin.</p>
      <p><strong>Why only Cloudflare?</strong> Workers, D1, R2 and cron are the whole stack, so there is nothing else to host. <a href="https://github.com/tidwick/tidwick/blob/main/docs/adr/0001-cloudflare-astro-platform.md">ADR 0001</a> has the reasoning.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
